WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.170
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.270 --> 00:02.200
[The characters, behaviors, locations, organizations, professions,

3
00:02.220 --> 00:04.150
and events depicted in this series are entirely fictional

4
00:04.170 --> 00:06.100
and created for entertainment purposes only.

5
00:06.120 --> 00:08.050
No harm or illegal action is intended to be promoted or encouraged.

6
00:08.070 --> 00:10.000
Viewer discretion is advised]

7
00:10.910 --> 00:12.080
Damn it, Jaab!

8
00:12.100 --> 00:13.720
Why did I fall for him?!

9
00:13.740 --> 00:14.680
Do you like Jane?

10
00:15.300 --> 00:16.200
Who's Jane?

11
00:16.240 --> 00:17.030
Oh, Mek?

12
00:17.050 --> 00:17.700
What brings you here?

13
00:17.720 --> 00:19.360
But I'm actually surprised that

14
00:19.380 --> 00:20.920
a goofball like you

15
00:21.130 --> 00:23.000
is serious about a relationship.

16
00:23.250 --> 00:25.440
I've never imagined that

17
00:25.870 --> 00:28.040
I'd have another close friend aside from Min.

18
00:28.170 --> 00:31.040
If she finds out, she must be really happy for you.

19
00:32.750 --> 00:34.040
Jane.

20
00:34.470 --> 00:35.480
I...

21
00:36.890 --> 00:37.890
like...

22
00:40.280 --> 00:41.600
Auntie Kaew! Auntie Kaew!

23
00:41.620 --> 00:42.520
Yes?

24
00:43.400 --> 00:45.600
- Ow! - Auntie Kaew!

25
00:46.920 --> 00:47.920
Master Jaab,

26
00:47.940 --> 00:51.000
you're amazing. You're the best.

27
00:51.020 --> 00:51.920
Auntie Kaew,

28
00:52.010 --> 00:53.800
let me know how many more you need.

29
00:53.820 --> 00:55.720
I'll pick them for you right away.

30
00:55.790 --> 00:58.160
Can I ask for one more?

31
00:58.320 --> 00:59.200
Just one more lime?

32
00:59.230 --> 00:59.960
One more orchard.

33
01:00.000 --> 01:01.590
- Huh?! An entire orchard?! - Mm.

34
01:01.610 --> 01:02.470
Yes, the whole orchard.

35
01:02.490 --> 01:03.720
Once we're done with the limes,

36
01:03.740 --> 01:05.710
I’ll have you pick some marian plums

37
01:05.740 --> 01:07.190
from those two orchards over there.

38
01:07.210 --> 01:10.100
Then come back here for some plum mangoes.

39
01:10.120 --> 01:11.400
Oh, what a shame.

40
01:11.420 --> 01:12.670
Longans aren't ready just yet.

41
01:12.690 --> 01:14.340
We would've had more fun

42
01:14.370 --> 01:15.520
going through four or five orchards of them.

43
01:16.700 --> 01:18.360
It's a shame, really.

44
01:19.200 --> 01:20.440
I was just joking!

45
01:21.640 --> 01:23.080
Auntie Kaew!

46
01:23.310 --> 01:25.640
You're quite a funny person, huh?

47
01:26.620 --> 01:28.160
I was joking about the longans.

48
01:28.310 --> 01:30.890
But I'm serious about the lime orchard.

49
01:31.300 --> 01:32.200
- Huh? - Here.

50
01:32.220 --> 01:33.690
You've only picked one lime.

51
01:33.710 --> 01:35.360
Come on. Let's get to it.

52
01:35.380 --> 01:36.220
- Then... - But Auntie Kaew...

53
01:36.240 --> 01:38.370
- Come on. - I've only managed to pick one.

54
01:38.390 --> 01:39.660
Get started with it.

55
01:39.680 --> 01:41.350
Just snip, snip, and snip those stems away.

56
01:41.370 --> 01:43.280
Just a few quick snips and you're done.

57
03:18.160 --> 03:19.520
How is it?

58
03:20.430 --> 03:21.470
Auntie...

59
03:21.960 --> 03:23.650
This mango is delicious.

60
03:23.900 --> 03:25.160
It's perfectly sweet and sour.

61
03:25.520 --> 03:26.540
I think this one is better.

62
03:26.560 --> 03:27.920
- Try it. - Alright.

63
03:31.170 --> 03:31.960
Mm!

64
03:32.190 --> 03:33.560
This one hits the spot,

65
03:33.620 --> 03:35.950
but the one before tastes better.

66
03:35.970 --> 03:37.200
Right.

67
03:37.320 --> 03:38.470
Oh, Auntie Kaew,

68
03:39.380 --> 03:40.500
I'm curious.

69
03:40.670 --> 03:43.570
Jane told me his family owns some orchards,

70
03:43.590 --> 03:45.280
but I don't know what kind of orchards they are.

71
03:45.460 --> 03:46.860
Many kinds of fruits are grown here.

72
03:47.460 --> 03:49.480
Mister and Madam...

73
03:50.920 --> 03:52.640
Master Jane's parents, I mean.

74
03:52.980 --> 03:55.840
They inherited this plot of land

75
03:56.080 --> 03:57.720
which stretches from this mountain

76
03:57.860 --> 04:00.460
all the way to another...

77
04:00.480 --> 04:01.360
Whoa, whoa.

78
04:01.780 --> 04:03.370
That's enough, Auntie.

79
04:03.400 --> 04:04.130
You can stop now.

80
04:04.150 --> 04:05.560
Does the land really stretch that far?

81
04:05.770 --> 04:07.940
Are you pulling my leg again?

82
04:09.120 --> 04:10.970
I'm being honest with you.

83
04:11.910 --> 04:14.970
The reason Master Jane never told you about this

84
04:15.210 --> 04:17.880
is probably because he couldn't count them all.

85
04:20.270 --> 04:21.630
He couldn't count all the mountains in the land?

86
04:21.650 --> 04:22.360
Right.

87
04:22.670 --> 04:24.920
And the rambutan, mangosteen, and the durian orchards

88
04:25.060 --> 04:27.130
are on that mountain. You need to drive to get there.

89
04:27.360 --> 04:28.070
Whoa.

90
04:28.090 --> 04:29.880
The ones that you can easily walk to

91
04:29.900 --> 04:32.610
- are the lime orchards you just saw. - Oh...

92
04:32.910 --> 04:34.060
Oh, there's also

93
04:34.170 --> 04:36.250
a sweet tamarind orchard in the backyard.

94
04:36.270 --> 04:37.530
There are all kinds of fruits here?

95
04:37.550 --> 04:39.040
There's a macadamia orchard, too.

96
04:39.150 --> 04:42.100
But we have to drive a long way up a mountain.

97
04:42.590 --> 04:43.300
Oh.

98
04:45.160 --> 04:45.920
My lord.

99
04:46.560 --> 04:49.460
If I’ve offended or bothered you,

100
04:49.680 --> 04:50.680
please...

101
04:50.960 --> 04:52.320
spare me.

102
04:56.360 --> 04:57.760
My lord.

103
04:58.460 --> 05:00.880
Please enjoy these fruits that Auntie Kaew

104
05:01.260 --> 05:02.330
and I...

105
05:02.350 --> 05:04.660
have harvested with our own hands. Please.

106
05:05.420 --> 05:06.480
Whoa, hold up.

107
05:08.060 --> 05:09.540
You must not get your hands dirty.

108
05:09.560 --> 05:11.360
Here. Allow me to feed you.

109
05:11.920 --> 05:14.240
Fresh off the tree. But it might be a bit salty.

110
05:14.260 --> 05:16.600
It's the saltiness from my hands. Now, please.

111
05:25.880 --> 05:26.690
How is it?

112
05:26.920 --> 05:27.710
It's exquisite, right?

113
05:27.730 --> 05:29.380
Right. I've been eating this since childhood.

114
05:29.400 --> 05:30.740
Yeah, I forgot.

115
05:30.760 --> 05:32.360
But I picked this one myself.

116
05:32.380 --> 05:33.730
The first one I've ever picked

117
05:33.960 --> 05:34.900
in my life.

118
05:34.920 --> 05:36.380
Here. One more bite.

119
05:41.180 --> 05:42.180
Jane.

120
05:42.760 --> 05:44.070
You really grew these yourself?

121
05:44.760 --> 05:45.890
I thought you could only find them overseas.

122
05:47.440 --> 05:48.880
They've been here for ages,

123
05:49.190 --> 05:50.680
even before I was born.

124
05:51.560 --> 05:53.400
They just have a fancy name.

125
05:53.870 --> 05:55.260
That's why people like you

126
05:55.850 --> 05:57.080
are often mistaken.

127
05:57.340 --> 05:57.990
Hey.

128
05:58.550 --> 05:59.970
What do you mean by that?

129
05:59.990 --> 06:00.720
Huh?!

130
06:03.480 --> 06:04.320
You...

131
06:04.860 --> 06:06.320
Are you calling me stupid?

132
06:06.460 --> 06:08.770
Oops. Did I accidentally say it out loud?

133
06:09.370 --> 06:10.370
You...

134
06:11.880 --> 06:13.670
There!

135
06:14.870 --> 06:16.200
Jaab, you teased me again.

136
06:16.320 --> 06:18.080
Well, you made fun of me first.

137
06:18.170 --> 06:20.120
I was just thinking it. I didn't say anything.

138
06:20.140 --> 06:21.080
There!

139
06:21.100 --> 06:23.240
You admitted it yourself that you wanted to roast me.

140
06:25.360 --> 06:28.070
I was born and raised in Bangkok.

141
06:28.090 --> 06:29.470
My house only has fences.

142
06:29.670 --> 06:30.910
There's only a simple lawn in my backyard,

143
06:30.930 --> 06:32.560
and a few random trees Mom planted.

144
06:32.750 --> 06:34.270
Who could ever be as talented

145
06:34.290 --> 06:36.850
and as knowledgeable

146
06:36.870 --> 06:39.400
as you who can enjoy the starry sky whenever you want?

147
06:40.020 --> 06:40.770
Huh?

148
06:43.920 --> 06:44.660
Hey.

149
06:45.140 --> 06:46.140
Be honest.

150
06:46.460 --> 06:47.800
Your life here is so comfortable.

151
06:48.470 --> 06:50.670
Why did you move to Bangkok to work for someone else?

152
06:54.500 --> 06:55.640
I just wanted to see

153
06:56.060 --> 06:58.320
what a starless night sky looked like.

154
06:59.580 --> 07:00.980
A starless night sky...

155
07:01.670 --> 07:03.120
is just a sky.

156
07:03.910 --> 07:05.000
It's ugly.

157
07:05.480 --> 07:07.150
The sky here is much more impressive.

158
07:09.990 --> 07:11.720
A starry night sky

159
07:12.020 --> 07:14.360
might feel special to some people,

160
07:15.380 --> 07:16.980
but the things that feel ordinary to them

161
07:17.680 --> 07:19.800
might also feel special to me.

162
07:22.660 --> 07:25.000
I grew up with all the things people might consider special.

163
07:26.190 --> 07:27.640
I live in a big house.

164
07:28.120 --> 07:29.780
I have massive orchards.

165
07:30.790 --> 07:32.560
I get to see starry night skies.

166
07:35.110 --> 07:36.440
But to me...

167
07:37.220 --> 07:39.220
getting to experience something new,

168
07:40.420 --> 07:42.310
moving into a condo,

169
07:42.330 --> 07:44.160
living in a high-rise,

170
07:44.860 --> 07:46.880
working with a lot of people,

171
07:47.750 --> 07:51.260
and being in such a chaotic and loud environment,

172
07:52.580 --> 07:54.920
all of these make my life a lot more fun.

173
07:56.060 --> 07:58.360
I've been in my own shell since forever.

174
07:59.400 --> 08:02.840
Deciding to enroll in a university on my own

175
08:03.550 --> 08:04.550
felt like...

176
08:05.170 --> 08:06.920
moving to a whole new world

177
08:07.840 --> 08:09.350
that I'd never known before.

178
08:11.280 --> 08:13.670
Even now, I must thank myself for being brave.

179
08:14.660 --> 08:16.340
What I’ve gained from all this

180
08:17.560 --> 08:18.860
is very valuable to me.

181
08:21.870 --> 08:23.840
That includes getting to know you, Jaab.

182
09:29.470 --> 09:30.960
I'm also happy

183
09:31.340 --> 09:32.640
that I got to know you, Jane.

184
10:25.540 --> 10:26.480
What are you doing?

185
10:31.820 --> 10:33.800
You woke up and immediately started messing around, Jane?

186
10:42.320 --> 10:43.800
You look funny like this, alright?

187
10:44.050 --> 10:44.880
Well...

188
10:45.280 --> 10:46.640
My body was doing its own thing.

189
10:46.660 --> 10:48.200
I don't know how I ended up like this.

190
10:50.760 --> 10:52.300
Next time, just ask.

191
10:52.320 --> 10:55.450
I told you there are plenty of isolated corners here.

192
10:55.470 --> 10:57.150
So that you won't have to lie around.

193
10:58.570 --> 11:00.240
Jeez.

194
11:01.240 --> 11:03.010
You were snoring in your sleep.

195
11:03.030 --> 11:04.390
Who would have the guts to wake you up?

196
11:04.420 --> 11:05.050
Ow!

197
11:05.070 --> 11:06.960
It was you who were snoring.

198
11:07.050 --> 11:09.180
Ow, Jane. Why did you hit me?

199
11:09.200 --> 11:11.350
That hurt. I think you just broke my arm.

200
11:11.370 --> 11:13.050
I can't work now.

201
11:14.760 --> 11:16.250
Hey, where are you going?

202
11:18.750 --> 11:19.760
Hey, Jane.

203
11:20.450 --> 11:21.730
You just woke up,

204
11:21.750 --> 11:22.940
and you're taking a nap already?

205
11:23.850 --> 11:24.950
It's my day off.

206
11:24.970 --> 11:26.040
What else do you want me to do?

207
11:33.240 --> 11:34.240
Of course.

208
11:34.560 --> 11:36.310
It's just me

209
11:36.470 --> 11:38.080
who has to work remotely.

210
11:39.070 --> 11:39.760
Jaab.

211
11:40.250 --> 11:40.990
Hm?

212
11:42.030 --> 11:43.600
Is it nice...

213
11:45.450 --> 11:46.480
having an older brother?

214
11:46.750 --> 11:47.840
Why did you ask?

215
11:51.010 --> 11:52.480
I'm just curious.

216
11:52.950 --> 11:55.080
Would it be nice to have one?

217
11:55.700 --> 11:57.800
And would it feel just like what I imagined?

218
11:57.960 --> 12:00.140
Jeng and I are eight years apart.

219
12:00.600 --> 12:02.860
That's pretty far apart for a pair of siblings.

220
12:04.330 --> 12:06.250
But being eight years older

221
12:06.840 --> 12:08.330
allowed Jeng to

222
12:08.350 --> 12:10.350
become Mom's golden boy

223
12:10.740 --> 12:12.560
and gave him all the company's work.

224
12:14.530 --> 12:15.600
You mean J. Group?

225
12:15.820 --> 12:16.710
Uh-huh.

226
12:17.630 --> 12:18.630
It's a good thing, though.

227
12:19.040 --> 12:21.040
I don't want that kind of job.

228
12:21.730 --> 12:24.000
I have to thank Jeng for being born before me.

229
12:24.150 --> 12:25.540
That's why I've been allowed to

230
12:25.740 --> 12:27.880
live such a messy life.

231
12:27.990 --> 12:28.830
Yeah.

232
12:28.850 --> 12:31.640
So my final answer is that

233
12:32.440 --> 12:33.240
it's nice to have one.

234
12:33.550 --> 12:34.820
It's so freaking nice.

235
12:36.750 --> 12:37.750
Even though...

236
12:38.040 --> 12:39.920
he complains so much as if he's my other dad,

237
12:40.160 --> 12:41.450
the good still outweighs the bad.

238
12:42.040 --> 12:43.680
So I'm cool with it.

239
12:44.060 --> 12:45.600
It's just like I thought, then.

240
12:45.720 --> 12:46.310
You...

241
12:47.530 --> 12:48.720
Are you alright, Jane?

242
12:56.280 --> 12:57.280
Jaab.

243
12:57.320 --> 12:59.080
See that orchard over there?

244
12:59.350 --> 13:00.340
Mm.

245
13:00.450 --> 13:01.660
You mean...

246
13:01.960 --> 13:03.550
from this mountain

247
13:03.570 --> 13:06.040
all the way to that one?

248
13:06.080 --> 13:07.110
Mm. There.

249
13:07.130 --> 13:08.830
All of that

250
13:08.850 --> 13:10.060
belongs to me.

251
13:10.550 --> 13:11.480
Whoa?!

252
13:11.520 --> 13:13.450
So you're a tycoon.

253
13:13.470 --> 13:15.820
Jeez, and I thought you took me here to do something with me.

254
13:15.840 --> 13:17.120
You just wanted to brag.

255
13:18.980 --> 13:20.720
I mean...

256
13:22.140 --> 13:23.440
In the future,

257
13:24.150 --> 13:26.520
everything here will become my responsibilities.

258
13:29.070 --> 13:30.650
The orchards,

259
13:30.850 --> 13:32.000
the workers,

260
13:32.150 --> 13:33.150
the plots of land,

261
13:33.930 --> 13:35.080
and...

262
13:37.340 --> 13:39.750
Dad's resort project that will open soon.

263
13:40.930 --> 13:43.950
I have to take care of everything myself.

264
13:47.840 --> 13:49.360
How will I handle them all?

265
13:53.440 --> 13:54.640
Hey, Jane.

266
13:56.420 --> 13:57.840
Are you okay?

267
13:58.290 --> 13:59.640
Do you know that...

268
14:00.240 --> 14:01.640
since the day I was born,

269
14:02.040 --> 14:04.760
my parents have spoiled me?

270
14:05.480 --> 14:06.960
Whatever school I wanted to go to,

271
14:07.140 --> 14:09.200
whatever I wanted to do or to have as my own,

272
14:09.750 --> 14:10.920
they let me have everything.

273
14:12.250 --> 14:13.880
But it was like buying time.

274
14:14.540 --> 14:17.080
Eventually, I’ll have to come back and work here.

275
14:23.150 --> 14:24.560
I'm jealous of you.

276
14:25.960 --> 14:27.440
Say...

277
14:28.060 --> 14:28.920
it'd be nice

278
14:29.250 --> 14:31.020
to have a brother like you do,

279
14:31.940 --> 14:33.080
right?

280
14:39.320 --> 14:41.920
If you want an older brother,

281
14:42.240 --> 14:44.860
I can find you one.

282
14:49.740 --> 14:50.880
Oh, but...

283
14:51.380 --> 14:52.960
He needs to help my dad with the orchards.

284
14:53.000 --> 14:54.680
I want somebody strong.

285
14:57.140 --> 14:58.850
I'm super jacked.

286
14:59.050 --> 15:00.950
I can carry tons of mangoes.

287
15:01.830 --> 15:02.830
But...

288
15:03.530 --> 15:05.000
this brother must supervise the workers, too.

289
15:05.240 --> 15:07.160
I'm looking for someone who's a bit stern.

290
15:07.260 --> 15:08.130
What do you think?

291
15:08.150 --> 15:09.150
Stern?

292
15:09.260 --> 15:10.800
- Yeah. - What the fuck do I do now?

293
15:12.900 --> 15:13.560
Hey!

294
15:14.740 --> 15:16.240
Anyone who has an issue with me,

295
15:16.590 --> 15:17.480
stand up!

296
15:20.360 --> 15:21.350
What are you laughing at?

297
15:21.540 --> 15:24.130
- I'm gonna hit you in the head... - Whoa.

298
15:24.160 --> 15:25.120
Jaab.

299
15:25.170 --> 15:27.000
It's me, Jane. Your brother.

300
15:27.080 --> 15:29.550
Oh, sorry. I forgot.

301
15:34.020 --> 15:34.960
Thank you.

302
15:35.340 --> 15:37.280
Huh? For what?

303
15:38.410 --> 15:39.850
You never stress me out

304
15:40.210 --> 15:42.040
whenever you're around.

305
16:02.580 --> 16:03.580
Do you know that...

306
16:03.960 --> 16:04.840
they call these

307
16:05.200 --> 16:07.320
kisses from an angel?

308
16:09.610 --> 16:11.640
You mean these dimples?

309
16:11.760 --> 16:12.560
Mm.

310
16:12.930 --> 16:15.320
They say those who have dimples are good people.

311
16:15.440 --> 16:17.850
An angel adored you, so she kissed you before you were born.

312
16:19.140 --> 16:20.140
Really?

313
16:20.160 --> 16:20.970
Mm.

314
16:23.470 --> 16:24.150
And...

315
16:24.480 --> 16:25.230
do you also...

316
16:25.540 --> 16:26.320
have them?

317
16:26.640 --> 16:28.040
The kisses from an angel?

318
16:28.440 --> 16:29.440
Um...

319
16:29.460 --> 16:30.400
I want to see.

320
16:32.560 --> 16:34.000
Do you have them? Let me see.

321
16:41.840 --> 16:42.740
Where are they?

322
16:42.760 --> 16:45.320
Please, Jaab. Show me.

323
16:45.660 --> 16:47.330
Please? Where? Where are they?

324
16:47.350 --> 16:49.040
Is it on this side? Or this?

325
16:51.980 --> 16:53.040
There!

326
16:53.530 --> 16:55.760
You also have a kiss from an angel.

327
16:56.050 --> 16:56.730
Here.

328
16:57.030 --> 16:58.080
It's just as soft.

329
16:59.730 --> 17:01.220
It's indented, huh?

330
17:02.860 --> 17:03.840
Jane.

331
17:06.180 --> 17:07.430
I know that I'm handsome,

332
17:07.450 --> 17:08.960
but can you not stare at me for too long?

333
17:09.440 --> 17:11.200
You're making me blush.

334
18:01.420 --> 18:02.420
Still awake?

335
18:04.030 --> 18:05.570
I'm preparing fruits,

336
18:05.590 --> 18:08.080
so you can bring them back to your condo.

337
18:08.100 --> 18:09.920
Oh, I prepared some for Master Jaab as well.

338
18:13.140 --> 18:14.930
And where is Jaab?

339
18:15.400 --> 18:16.840
He just went inside.

340
18:22.750 --> 18:23.420
Auntie Kaew.

341
18:23.440 --> 18:24.220
Yes?

342
18:26.240 --> 18:27.940
Do you think...

343
18:28.320 --> 18:29.230
Jaab

344
18:29.740 --> 18:30.680
is talented?

345
18:32.030 --> 18:33.030
Of course, he is.

346
18:33.540 --> 18:35.320
Very talented.

347
18:35.340 --> 18:38.110
I just found out he’s a director.

348
18:38.720 --> 18:42.230
He showed me a lot of his work, too.

349
18:42.590 --> 18:44.120
Then I realized that

350
18:44.150 --> 18:46.830
I've seen some of the ads he directed while I was watching soap operas.

351
18:47.030 --> 18:48.920
I never knew those were his work.

352
18:51.350 --> 18:53.220
Not only is he good at his job,

353
18:53.430 --> 18:55.400
but he's also great with people.

354
18:57.030 --> 18:58.030
Like...

355
18:58.530 --> 19:00.250
he only knew you for a little while,

356
19:00.930 --> 19:02.360
and he already made you love him.

357
19:04.440 --> 19:05.740
And what about you?

358
19:07.220 --> 19:08.560
Do you love him?

359
19:20.540 --> 19:22.560
It's fine if you don't want to answer me.

360
19:35.520 --> 19:36.230
Hey.

361
19:37.110 --> 19:38.750
Is this yours and Jane's idea, Auntie Kaew?

362
19:38.770 --> 19:39.390
Hm?

363
19:39.920 --> 19:40.730
What idea?

364
19:40.750 --> 19:41.320
Well,

365
19:41.340 --> 19:42.740
your plan is to turn me

366
19:42.760 --> 19:44.520
into a pest like Jane!

367
19:46.150 --> 19:47.150
Auntie Kaew.

368
19:47.170 --> 19:48.600
- Yes? - I'll be honest with you.

369
19:48.620 --> 19:49.770
If there was one more carton,

370
19:49.790 --> 19:51.840
I could set up a stall and sell the fruit at my condo.

371
19:52.000 --> 19:53.820
Would you like some more? I'll have the workers handle it.

372
19:53.850 --> 19:56.100
- Anybody! Bring him some more! - Oh, Auntie Kaew. Auntie, I...

373
19:56.120 --> 19:58.040
I was just joking. Jeez...

374
19:58.630 --> 20:00.100
I can't tease you at all, huh?

375
20:00.120 --> 20:01.030
Gosh.

376
20:01.250 --> 20:03.540
Don't tease an elder like that.

377
20:03.560 --> 20:05.450
I thought you were being serious.

378
20:05.470 --> 20:06.410
Goodness.

379
20:14.640 --> 20:17.120
Have a safe journey, Master Jane.

380
20:17.330 --> 20:18.230
Thank you.

381
20:19.030 --> 20:21.270
Take care of yourself, Auntie Kaew.

382
20:21.290 --> 20:22.960
I'll come home often.

383
20:24.740 --> 20:26.830
Enjoy your life.

384
20:27.540 --> 20:30.440
Come home when you're exhausted or tired.

385
20:31.050 --> 20:32.340
- Mm. - Right.

386
20:35.550 --> 20:37.250
Take care of yourself.

387
20:37.270 --> 20:38.520
I will.

388
20:43.990 --> 20:45.120
Master Jaab.

389
20:45.230 --> 20:45.840
Yes?

390
20:46.120 --> 20:48.480
Yes, you. Come here.

391
20:50.230 --> 20:51.330
Me too?

392
20:51.350 --> 20:53.080
- Yes, Master Jaab. Come here.

393
20:58.360 --> 21:01.280
Lend me a hand again the next time you're here, okay?

394
21:02.360 --> 21:03.730
Of course, Auntie Kaew.

395
21:03.750 --> 21:04.750
Next time,

396
21:05.850 --> 21:09.320
I'll get even more jacked so I can help you carry stuff!

397
21:09.360 --> 21:10.710
Whoa...

398
21:10.730 --> 21:12.800
With all these muscles,

399
21:12.820 --> 21:14.720
you should come help me during the durian season.

400
21:14.760 --> 21:15.390
Yes.

401
21:15.410 --> 21:17.120
You'll get to carry tons of them like you said.

402
21:18.950 --> 21:19.710
Durians, huh?

403
21:19.730 --> 21:20.800
Exactly.

404
21:21.240 --> 21:22.740
They're heavy, you know?

405
21:28.240 --> 21:30.350
Take care and travel safely, dear.

406
21:30.370 --> 21:31.340
Thank you.

407
21:33.520 --> 21:34.510
See you, Auntie Kaew.

408
21:34.530 --> 21:35.410
Right.

409
21:37.280 --> 21:38.600
Wait until it's the durian season...

410
21:38.620 --> 21:40.440
Don't forget to put on your seatbelts.

411
21:40.460 --> 21:41.320
- Yes. - Alright.

412
21:47.540 --> 21:48.940
Bye-bye.

413
22:06.050 --> 22:08.130
You can leave my stuff in front of the lobby.

414
22:08.150 --> 22:10.280
Looks like I'll have to... come back for another load.

415
22:10.470 --> 22:11.340
Wait, why...

416
22:11.830 --> 22:13.440
Why make two trips?

417
22:14.140 --> 22:15.360
I'll help.

418
22:15.730 --> 22:17.180
Oh, okay.

419
22:17.630 --> 22:18.640
Yeah.

420
22:19.360 --> 22:20.120
Let's go.

421
22:39.550 --> 22:41.040
I guess I'll...

422
22:41.530 --> 22:43.160
I'll leave it here.

423
22:43.830 --> 22:44.830
Aren't you gonna come inside?

424
22:46.340 --> 22:47.060
Huh?

425
22:47.940 --> 22:50.720
So you can take your hoodie back. It's dry and clean now.

426
22:52.230 --> 22:53.240
Inside?

427
22:57.020 --> 22:59.230
Sure! Of course, Jane.

428
22:59.250 --> 22:59.980
I'll...

429
23:06.550 --> 23:08.080
You can put that down right there.

430
23:21.450 --> 23:22.640
- Here. - Whoa!

431
23:25.150 --> 23:26.110
Oh.

432
23:27.240 --> 23:28.720
Thank you, Jane.

433
23:29.740 --> 23:31.720
Oh, it smells really nice.

434
23:31.750 --> 23:33.640
I guess I should go now.

435
23:34.520 --> 23:35.440
Wait.

436
23:40.330 --> 23:42.030
What... What is it, Jane?

437
23:42.740 --> 23:43.740
Aren't you gonna drink some water?

438
23:44.630 --> 23:45.630
Drink...

439
23:45.650 --> 23:46.630
Oh.

440
23:46.830 --> 23:48.050
Oh, I...

441
23:48.450 --> 23:49.510
I already had some water on the drive here.

442
23:50.700 --> 23:51.890
All done. Then, I...

443
23:51.910 --> 23:53.400
I'm gonna go now.

444
23:54.540 --> 23:57.680
Jane... Why did you get up?

445
23:58.040 --> 23:59.050
To send you off, obviously.

446
24:00.130 --> 24:01.740
Oh, to send me off.

447
24:02.930 --> 24:04.630
It's okay, Jane. Uh...

448
24:05.240 --> 24:06.160
My car.

449
24:06.570 --> 24:07.640
I parked it at the front.

450
24:07.660 --> 24:09.260
It's right next to the elevator.

451
24:09.280 --> 24:10.840
I can go on my own.

452
24:30.320 --> 24:31.930
You don't need a key card to go down.

453
24:31.950 --> 24:33.400
Press G and you're good to go.

454
24:33.520 --> 24:34.520
Okay.

455
24:36.440 --> 24:37.360
Jane.

456
24:37.870 --> 24:38.640
Hm?

457
24:38.660 --> 24:40.080
Thank you for...

458
24:40.840 --> 24:41.920
bringing me to your house.

459
24:42.640 --> 24:43.960
Thank you, too,

460
24:44.530 --> 24:45.930
for making it a lot more fun back home.

461
24:46.620 --> 24:47.760
We should go back there sometime.

462
24:48.860 --> 24:51.830
Whoa, don't just say that.

463
24:52.120 --> 24:53.680
I'll go if you say so.

464
24:56.840 --> 24:57.920
I'm being serious.

465
25:05.720 --> 25:06.720
Okay.

466
25:07.220 --> 25:08.200
It's a deal, then.

467
25:08.630 --> 25:09.960
Well...

468
25:10.160 --> 25:11.880
Tell me when you're back at your condo.

469
25:14.040 --> 25:15.040
Drive safely.

470
25:15.060 --> 25:15.920
Bye.

471
25:31.050 --> 25:31.920
Am I...

472
25:33.040 --> 25:34.640
Do I really like Jane?

473
25:35.730 --> 25:37.050
Do I like Jane...?

474
25:39.640 --> 25:41.480
Do I actually like him?

475
25:48.400 --> 25:50.040
Yeah, I do. I like Jane.

476
25:54.730 --> 25:56.210
See? I told you.

477
25:56.230 --> 25:57.180
Yeah.

478
25:57.200 --> 25:59.150
I can see actual hearts in his eyes, Mek.

479
25:59.820 --> 26:01.360
You're right.

480
26:01.650 --> 26:03.680
There are hearts everywhere.

481
26:04.830 --> 26:07.400
Give us a quick recap. What happened in Phetchabun?

482
26:08.720 --> 26:10.160
What happened there...?

483
26:10.960 --> 26:11.840
Well...

484
26:12.620 --> 26:15.480
The trip was full of cuteness!

485
26:15.570 --> 26:16.480
Ugh...

486
26:17.890 --> 26:18.760
What the hell?

487
26:19.030 --> 26:19.850
Guys!

488
26:19.870 --> 26:20.480
What?

489
26:20.960 --> 26:21.960
I think...

490
26:23.170 --> 26:24.800
I'm gonna make a move on Jane.

491
26:26.660 --> 26:27.760
Can I do that?

492
26:27.780 --> 26:29.600
Hey, and... where do you think

493
26:29.620 --> 26:31.020
we should go for our first date?

494
26:31.040 --> 26:32.920
How about... we go to the movies?

495
26:32.940 --> 26:35.900
Or should we make merit at some temple?

496
26:35.920 --> 26:37.130
How about I take him to...

497
26:37.150 --> 26:39.280
a zoo?! Dusit Zoo?

498
26:49.920 --> 26:53.960
[Good night, Jane]

499
27:07.730 --> 27:08.440
Jane...

500
27:09.340 --> 27:10.200
Fucking hell!

501
27:10.220 --> 27:11.520
What the fuck were you dreaming about, handsome?

502
27:12.430 --> 27:13.640
Why the fuck are you sitting here?

503
27:13.660 --> 27:15.520
Well, Jane isn't here yet.

504
27:15.650 --> 27:17.180
Can't I just have a moment with you first?

505
27:17.200 --> 27:19.030
A moment, my ass. You're creepy!

506
27:19.650 --> 27:22.440
Well, when are you making your first move?

507
27:23.880 --> 27:25.070
The fuck you mean my first move?

508
27:25.090 --> 27:28.160
Well, you told me that you liked Jane yesterday, didn't you?

509
27:32.010 --> 27:34.000
Jaab, do you have a crush on Jane?

510
27:51.360 --> 27:53.940
What? Calm down. Why are you dragging me here?!

511
27:53.960 --> 27:57.000
You two must keep this a secret!

512
27:57.600 --> 27:59.090
You mean the fact that you have a crush on Jane?

513
27:59.110 --> 28:00.490
Take that, Pun!

514
28:00.510 --> 28:01.560
I told you to keep quiet!

515
28:02.520 --> 28:04.840
Okay. I won't say that you like Jane again.

516
28:05.700 --> 28:06.550
Damn it, Pun.

517
28:06.570 --> 28:07.760
While I was telling you to shut up,

518
28:07.780 --> 28:09.880
you said it out loud twice. Do you know that, bastard?!

519
28:11.340 --> 28:12.410
Uh, but...

520
28:12.430 --> 28:15.440
The more people know about this, the better it is for you, isn't that right?

521
28:15.540 --> 28:16.720
Better, my ass.

522
28:16.740 --> 28:17.720
Jane will feel uncomfortable.

523
28:18.630 --> 28:20.850
But you're making a move on him, no?

524
28:20.870 --> 28:23.400
You have to let Jane know that you like him, right?

525
28:25.530 --> 28:27.800
Yeah, I know. But...

526
28:28.230 --> 28:29.720
I need to make a plan first.

527
28:29.740 --> 28:30.680
I don't want to rush in.

528
28:31.340 --> 28:33.710
When you said you didn't want to "rush in..."

529
28:33.730 --> 28:35.840
Does it actually mean that...

530
28:36.230 --> 28:37.120
you're a chicken?

531
28:37.850 --> 28:39.480
Um... A chicken?

532
28:39.560 --> 28:41.350
- Khanoon, buddy! - Ow, what is it?

533
28:41.370 --> 28:42.230
Chicken, my ass.

534
28:42.250 --> 28:43.480
Damn it.

535
28:44.840 --> 28:45.840
I get you.

536
28:46.240 --> 28:49.200
This stuff takes time, right?

537
28:49.340 --> 28:50.120
Yeah, no shit!

538
28:50.330 --> 28:52.400
You should've understood that a long time ago.

539
28:52.420 --> 28:53.840
Why did you have to make me panic?

540
28:54.620 --> 28:55.920
By the way...

541
28:57.040 --> 28:59.600
when did the two of you feel the first spark?

542
29:02.850 --> 29:04.360
The two of us, my ass.

543
29:04.720 --> 29:06.600
It's just me alone who felt the spark.

544
29:07.070 --> 29:07.760
Well...

545
29:07.960 --> 29:09.040
It's been a while now.

546
29:09.060 --> 29:09.910
But...

547
29:09.930 --> 29:12.360
it became clear for me when we got back from Phetchabun.

548
29:14.350 --> 29:15.440
And do you think he has feelings for you?

549
29:16.740 --> 29:17.740
What are you talking about?

550
29:18.520 --> 29:19.730
How would I know?

551
29:19.760 --> 29:20.600
Huh?!

552
29:20.780 --> 29:22.280
How can you not know?

553
29:22.540 --> 29:25.330
You two were alone together for two nights.

554
29:25.360 --> 29:26.600
Did you do anything that might have

555
29:27.240 --> 29:28.640
ignited the romance?

556
29:29.450 --> 29:30.560
I don't know.

557
29:30.720 --> 29:33.200
I actually feel that way all the time.

558
29:34.960 --> 29:35.960
On your own?

559
29:36.140 --> 29:39.040
I'm talking about Jane.

560
29:39.170 --> 29:41.700
Did Jane do something that made you go...

561
29:42.430 --> 29:44.040
like, "What the hell?!"

562
29:44.060 --> 29:45.700
Or did he make you question yourself like, "Huh?!"

563
29:46.420 --> 29:50.020
Like something we never did after being friends for a decade?

564
29:50.040 --> 29:50.680
Did he?

565
29:51.030 --> 29:53.800
Something we never did?

566
30:06.060 --> 30:07.320
- Khanoon. - Hm?

567
30:07.680 --> 30:09.560
I don't want to get my hopes up.

568
30:10.600 --> 30:11.540
Hey.

569
30:11.840 --> 30:14.040
You're overthinking it.

570
30:14.250 --> 30:15.300
You're overthinking...

571
30:15.940 --> 30:17.840
so much that your tiny little brain

572
30:18.000 --> 30:20.040
is now overloaded.

573
30:21.820 --> 30:24.040
But Jane...

574
30:24.240 --> 30:25.560
Pun!

575
30:25.990 --> 30:27.530
How many times have I told you to shut up?

576
30:29.560 --> 30:30.330
Hey...

577
30:30.360 --> 30:32.810
So you and I are in the same boat, huh?

578
30:32.830 --> 30:35.470
From now on, if I tell you to "go left," then you must go left.

579
30:35.490 --> 30:37.420
If I tell you to "go right," then you must go right.

580
30:37.450 --> 30:39.160
You must be a good supporter.

581
30:39.540 --> 30:40.540
Understood?

582
30:40.560 --> 30:41.440
Okay.

583
30:41.620 --> 30:42.400
Excellent.

584
30:42.550 --> 30:44.480
Are you done chatting? Bew told me to fetch you.

585
30:50.350 --> 30:52.840
I was gonna tell you that Jane was walking toward us.

586
30:52.870 --> 30:53.620
I wasn't gonna say that

587
30:53.640 --> 30:54.610
you have a crush on...

588
30:54.630 --> 30:56.250
- Hey! Ow. - Stop! Stop it!

589
30:56.270 --> 30:57.170
We were...

590
30:57.190 --> 30:58.690
- talking about something... - No... I mean, yeah.

591
30:58.710 --> 31:02.210
- Uh... About cryptocurrency. - Cryptocurrency.

592
31:02.230 --> 31:03.660
- Yeah, yeah. - It was completely green.

593
31:03.680 --> 31:05.000
- He's right... Hey. - Correct.

594
31:05.020 --> 31:07.300
- Would you like to join us, Jane? - Exactly.

595
31:07.330 --> 31:09.100
Pun, our dear brother, wants to discuss it.

596
31:09.120 --> 31:11.120
- So the three of us are talking. - Right. He wants money more than we do.

597
31:11.140 --> 31:12.080
He’s desperate for cash.

598
31:14.370 --> 31:17.200
This is Ai. Today is his first day of internship here

599
31:17.230 --> 31:18.440
as a PD.

600
31:19.530 --> 31:22.000
- Hello, my name is Ai. - Hi.

601
31:22.570 --> 31:23.330
Alright.

602
31:23.540 --> 31:24.670
That's Jane.

603
31:24.700 --> 31:28.750
He’s the nicest PD on the team.

604
31:28.780 --> 31:31.600
You're very lucky to work with him.

605
31:32.010 --> 31:33.430
Oh, Sis.

606
31:33.930 --> 31:34.930
What about me?

607
31:35.050 --> 31:36.600
Am I not your good boy?

608
31:36.820 --> 31:39.000
- Sheesh. - Since when did I stop being your best boy?

609
31:40.030 --> 31:40.930
And that is...

610
31:40.960 --> 31:42.600
Chomphoo, one of the assistants.

611
31:42.820 --> 31:44.240
- Hi, dear. - Hello.

612
31:44.760 --> 31:46.520
This is our director, Jaab.

613
31:46.720 --> 31:48.520
- Hi there. - Hello.

614
31:48.910 --> 31:49.840
That's Pun.

615
31:50.240 --> 31:51.240
Hello.

616
31:51.750 --> 31:53.020
Hi.

617
31:53.040 --> 31:54.120
I'm Pun.

618
31:54.150 --> 31:55.600
Right. Hi.

619
32:00.240 --> 32:03.320
This is pretty much most of our team.

620
32:03.540 --> 32:05.960
And we outsource people for support.

621
32:07.020 --> 32:08.700
- What the hell? - Oh.

622
32:08.720 --> 32:10.220
What about me?!

623
32:10.240 --> 32:14.160
I'm the best DOP on the pink team!

624
32:14.410 --> 32:15.410
Well, there.

625
32:15.530 --> 32:18.600
You've already introduced yourself. I have nothing left to say now.

626
32:18.660 --> 32:20.820
- She's right. - My introduction isn't as fancy as the others.

627
32:20.850 --> 32:22.790
- It's Khanoon, alright? - Hello.

628
32:22.810 --> 32:24.830
It's a pleasure to meet you all.

629
32:24.850 --> 32:27.590
If you need anything, please call me anytime.

630
32:27.610 --> 32:30.250
Alright. You can sit next to Pun.

631
32:30.280 --> 32:31.320
And...

632
32:32.350 --> 32:34.200
If you need anything, they will assist you.

633
32:34.230 --> 32:35.680
- Alright. - Yes.

634
32:37.690 --> 32:39.350
You can sit next to Pun.

635
32:39.950 --> 32:41.310
- Thank you. - Hey.

636
32:41.910 --> 32:43.490
Well, he's new here.

637
32:43.510 --> 32:45.540
- That's good. Take care of him. - It's our job to look after him.

638
32:45.570 --> 32:47.150
Not just looking after him, though.

639
32:47.170 --> 32:48.510
Since he's our newest member,

640
32:48.530 --> 32:50.380
we need to throw him a welcome party, right?

641
32:50.410 --> 32:51.320
Hey.

642
32:51.340 --> 32:53.830
That's a reasonable thing to do.

643
32:53.940 --> 32:54.840
Of course.

644
32:55.020 --> 32:56.020
What now, Sis?

645
32:56.610 --> 32:57.610
Um...

646
32:58.250 --> 33:01.960
Tonight. At the same karaoke bar we hosted Jane's welcome party.

647
33:02.330 --> 33:04.550
- Yay! - Yay!

648
33:04.570 --> 33:05.840
That's more like it!

649
33:06.040 --> 33:07.640
Amazing. That's the spirit.

650
33:08.620 --> 33:09.230
Jane.

651
33:09.250 --> 33:09.810
Hm?

652
33:09.830 --> 33:11.120
Help me keep the mic safe.

653
33:11.450 --> 33:13.420
Don't let Khanoon take it.

654
33:13.440 --> 33:15.440
Oh, you'll regret saying that.

655
33:15.650 --> 33:17.540
I'll be seeing you tonight, then.

656
33:17.560 --> 33:19.350
Whoa, Khanoon. Why wait until tonight?

657
33:19.370 --> 33:21.820
- How about we settle it right here? Damn it. - Come on, then.

658
33:21.840 --> 33:23.800
- Hey. - Sorry, sorry, sorry.

659
33:24.160 --> 33:26.260
- Three, two, one! - Come on.

660
33:26.340 --> 33:27.330
Just kidding.

661
33:27.350 --> 33:29.960
- Our team doesn't condone violence. - Exactly.

662
33:29.980 --> 33:32.130
- No shit. - We usually work hard.

663
33:34.810 --> 33:37.350
Let's grab some food at the entrance of the alley.

664
33:37.370 --> 33:39.140
If you want to have lunch there,

665
33:39.160 --> 33:41.570
or if you don't have your own lunch with you, join us.

666
33:41.590 --> 33:42.670
- Mm. - Okay?

667
33:43.370 --> 33:45.690
Eat up. Make sure you enjoy it, too.

668
33:45.720 --> 33:47.680
Sis is rarely this generous.

669
33:48.040 --> 33:49.430
Hey, Sis!

670
33:52.680 --> 33:54.080
It's to welcome him.

671
33:54.140 --> 33:56.980
What's wrong? Are you arguing with the fridge?

672
33:58.450 --> 33:59.450
Jane!

673
34:01.250 --> 34:02.200
What is it?

674
34:03.070 --> 34:06.160
I...want to share my fruits with Ai.

675
34:06.180 --> 34:08.680
Which one of these do you think he will like...?

676
34:09.890 --> 34:10.890
I don't know.

677
34:11.190 --> 34:12.190
Why don't you ask him?

678
34:12.220 --> 34:13.120
Ai...

679
34:14.980 --> 34:17.440
I'm too nervous to talk to him.

680
34:18.070 --> 34:20.040
I'm afraid he wouldn't like any of these.

681
34:20.060 --> 34:21.560
I have nothing else to give him either.

682
34:21.870 --> 34:24.560
Oh, you introvert.

683
34:24.980 --> 34:26.330
I don't really get it,

684
34:26.360 --> 34:27.470
but I kinda do.

685
34:27.880 --> 34:30.040
How about this? Don't worry.

686
34:30.060 --> 34:31.320
I'll handle it for you.

687
34:33.890 --> 34:34.890
Ai.

688
34:34.910 --> 34:35.840
Yes, Jaab?

689
34:36.160 --> 34:38.960
Jane wants to share his fruits with you...

690
34:38.980 --> 34:39.880
Do you want some?

691
34:40.640 --> 34:42.930
He has mangoes,

692
34:42.960 --> 34:44.600
longans, grapes,

693
34:44.640 --> 34:45.860
apples, and guavas.

694
34:45.880 --> 34:46.460
Do you want anything?

695
34:46.480 --> 34:47.780
I can try any of them.

696
34:47.800 --> 34:48.980
I love fruits.

697
34:49.000 --> 34:50.520
Oh, so you're easy to feed.

698
34:53.760 --> 34:54.760
Let's see, Jane.

699
34:58.020 --> 34:59.500
Here. I'll help.

700
35:09.340 --> 35:10.140
Here.

701
35:10.740 --> 35:12.240
This one is all yours.

702
35:12.280 --> 35:14.560
Auntie Kaew said not to share it with anyone.

703
35:18.530 --> 35:20.200
This looks amazing, Jane.

704
35:21.480 --> 35:22.960
Don't get ahead of yourself.

705
35:24.170 --> 35:25.680
Don't, my ass.

706
35:28.450 --> 35:30.600
Are these from your orchards?

707
35:30.640 --> 35:32.860
- Some of them are. - Mm.

708
35:32.880 --> 35:34.470
But they're all organic.

709
35:34.490 --> 35:36.120
I got them from my fellow orchard owners.

710
35:36.330 --> 35:37.280
These are huge.

711
35:37.300 --> 35:38.580
They look amazing.

712
35:39.530 --> 35:40.840
I'm not trying to brag or anything,

713
35:40.860 --> 35:41.860
but this guy!

714
35:41.880 --> 35:43.000
The person in front of you here,

715
35:43.250 --> 35:44.910
owns the entire Phetchabun province.

716
35:44.930 --> 35:45.920
- Huh?! - What?

717
35:46.550 --> 35:47.800
You own...

718
35:47.830 --> 35:49.400
the entire province?

719
35:49.540 --> 35:50.240
No, I don't!

720
35:50.270 --> 35:51.220
Are you part of the royal family?

721
35:51.240 --> 35:51.900
No.

722
35:51.920 --> 35:53.720
Are you from an elite clan?

723
35:54.760 --> 35:55.930
That's a good guess.

724
35:55.950 --> 35:58.400
The design of his house is like...

725
35:58.560 --> 36:00.480
You're misleading everyone, Jaab.

726
36:01.450 --> 36:04.040
I think Jane is an ordinary person.

727
36:04.970 --> 36:06.680
But he's an ordinary person who is...

728
36:07.160 --> 36:07.760
wealthy.

729
36:09.350 --> 36:10.800
It's not like that, Ai.

730
36:11.360 --> 36:13.000
Don't get me wrong.

731
36:13.340 --> 36:16.330
But if you walked in from the entrance,

732
36:16.350 --> 36:17.950
and you brought grapes with you,

733
36:17.970 --> 36:19.320
by the time you reached the actual house,

734
36:19.340 --> 36:20.800
those grapes would've already turned into wine.

735
36:20.830 --> 36:21.910
It's so vast.

736
36:21.930 --> 36:23.030
Shit. Are you serious?

737
36:23.050 --> 36:24.320
- Really? - Wine, you say?

738
36:25.460 --> 36:26.540
So his place is massive.

739
36:26.570 --> 36:28.840
I want to visit there now.

740
36:28.860 --> 36:30.520
Will you come? You'll have a good time.

741
36:30.550 --> 36:32.060
There are so many things to do.

742
36:32.090 --> 36:33.480
- Can I go? - Sure.

743
36:34.980 --> 36:36.580
There's a beautiful water reservoir, too.

744
36:36.600 --> 36:39.240
The evening vibe there is amazing, and the sunset is stunning.

745
36:52.160 --> 36:53.360
Anything I can help?

746
36:54.140 --> 36:55.140
Oh...

747
36:55.460 --> 36:56.460
Well...

748
36:56.660 --> 36:59.720
I tried to print it out. There were some rattling noises,

749
36:59.740 --> 37:02.800
but nothing came out.

750
37:03.070 --> 37:03.960
Oh...

751
37:04.540 --> 37:05.840
The paper is probably jammed.

752
37:06.350 --> 37:07.930
Let me see what I can do.

753
37:07.950 --> 37:08.950
Sure.

754
37:26.350 --> 37:27.350
Yay!

755
37:27.370 --> 37:28.640
It worked.

756
37:28.740 --> 37:31.520
You're this happy over something so small?

757
37:31.640 --> 37:32.400
Uh...

758
37:32.960 --> 37:33.960
Well...

759
37:34.060 --> 37:36.070
Without your help,

760
37:36.090 --> 37:38.360
I wouldn't have figured it out.

761
37:38.390 --> 37:39.800
Like...

762
37:40.970 --> 37:43.240
I didn't want to bother the others, too.

763
37:43.440 --> 37:46.150
Actually, everyone here is happy to help.

764
37:46.170 --> 37:47.600
Feel free to ask around.

765
37:47.860 --> 37:49.080
Oh.

766
37:50.120 --> 37:51.480
I'm the kindest person here, though.

767
37:51.970 --> 37:53.920
Tell me if you need help.

768
37:54.150 --> 37:56.120
Oh, it's fine.

769
37:56.270 --> 37:58.240
I'm a PD intern.

770
37:58.260 --> 38:01.120
Bew said Jane is my supervisor.

771
38:01.450 --> 38:02.240
I guess...

772
38:02.470 --> 38:04.240
PDs and PMs do pretty similar work.

773
38:04.470 --> 38:05.760
We can help each other out,

774
38:06.170 --> 38:09.120
since we sit next to each other.

775
38:09.690 --> 38:12.320
Oh. Thank you, Pun.

776
38:12.460 --> 38:13.200
And...

777
38:13.870 --> 38:15.160
how are you going to the karaoke bar?

778
38:15.240 --> 38:16.950
I'm not sure, actually.

779
38:16.970 --> 38:19.800
I think I'm gonna hitch a ride with someone here.

780
38:22.740 --> 38:24.880
Can that someone be me?

781
38:25.470 --> 38:26.040
Yes?

782
38:28.250 --> 38:29.800
My car has some available seats.

783
38:30.260 --> 38:31.460
Several ones, actually.

784
38:33.250 --> 38:34.250
Oh.

785
38:37.170 --> 38:38.840
I'll take that smile as a yes.

786
38:51.660 --> 38:54.590
Uh... I need to get back to work now.

787
38:54.610 --> 38:55.400
Oh.

788
38:56.650 --> 38:58.550
- Sure. - Thank you.

789
38:58.950 --> 38:59.950
Go ahead.

790
39:07.120 --> 39:08.850
One, two, three, four! [Intern Welcome Party]

791
39:22.070 --> 39:22.960
Alright. Come on!

792
39:34.270 --> 39:35.280
Ai.

793
39:35.780 --> 39:36.600
Yes?

794
39:36.960 --> 39:38.600
How was your first day?

795
39:39.150 --> 39:40.240
Oh...

796
39:40.460 --> 39:41.460
It went well.

797
39:41.840 --> 39:44.520
Working at the office was much more fun than I thought.

798
39:45.240 --> 39:46.720
I'm feeling less nervous now.

799
39:55.750 --> 39:57.000
Is there something on your mind, Jane?

800
40:01.670 --> 40:05.080
Jaab told me to confess.

801
40:06.350 --> 40:07.240
Huh?

802
40:07.740 --> 40:08.720
Confess?

803
40:16.160 --> 40:18.160
What do I do?

804
40:27.940 --> 40:29.470
- Ow! Ow! - Oh?

805
40:29.750 --> 40:30.960
Was that you, Jane?

806
40:30.990 --> 40:32.060
Where are you?

807
40:32.080 --> 40:32.960
Jaab!

808
40:33.250 --> 40:34.280
- Oh! - It hurts!

809
40:40.850 --> 40:41.880
Are you alright?

810
40:44.740 --> 40:45.680
I'm fine.

811
40:45.740 --> 40:46.680
Oh.

812
40:46.960 --> 40:49.550
You're frowning like wilted vegetables,

813
40:49.570 --> 40:50.840
and you're telling me you're fine?

814
40:54.270 --> 40:56.360
I've never been a supervisor before, Jaab.

815
40:57.260 --> 41:00.000
Are you...stressed about Ai?

816
41:00.640 --> 41:01.680
Mm.

817
41:02.840 --> 41:04.950
- What should I do? - Aww...

818
41:05.100 --> 41:07.020
Come here. It's okay.

819
41:07.040 --> 41:09.050
Don't cry, Jane.

820
41:09.070 --> 41:11.560
- There, there, there. - I'm worried he'd feel uncomfortable.

821
41:11.750 --> 41:13.480
I'm not that social.

822
41:14.780 --> 41:16.560
I'm worried he'd think that I'm strict

823
41:16.820 --> 41:18.640
and that I refuse to teach him about work.

824
41:20.670 --> 41:22.640
How am I supposed to mentor anyone?

825
41:23.060 --> 41:24.780
I can't even take care of myself.

826
41:26.150 --> 41:27.850
How about you be direct with him?

827
41:27.870 --> 41:29.360
I think he'll understand.

828
41:31.320 --> 41:32.330
What should I tell him?

829
41:32.350 --> 41:33.670
Just tell him that

830
41:33.700 --> 41:35.280
"I'm not good at talking,

831
41:35.560 --> 41:37.470
but I'm not strict."

832
41:37.490 --> 41:38.480
Something like that.

833
41:38.960 --> 41:41.120
Whatever you think will make him uncomfortable,

834
41:41.140 --> 41:42.760
just say it to him right away.

835
41:44.720 --> 41:46.840
You always take an easy way out, huh?

836
41:47.070 --> 41:48.160
Huh, Jane?

837
41:49.240 --> 41:50.320
That was a compliment.

838
41:51.550 --> 41:53.000
Spending time with you

839
41:53.570 --> 41:55.760
makes my life seem a lot simpler.

840
41:57.440 --> 41:59.360
Stay with me for a long time, okay?

841
41:59.550 --> 42:00.640
Don't leave.

842
42:03.550 --> 42:05.760
If you don't tell me to leave, then I won't.

843
42:05.950 --> 42:07.250
And even if you tell me to leave,

844
42:07.270 --> 42:09.170
I won't.

845
42:09.190 --> 42:11.140
If I were to leave,

846
42:11.160 --> 42:13.450
I wouldn't be able to squeeze your cheeks like this.

847
42:13.470 --> 42:14.640
There. Like this.

848
42:14.860 --> 42:16.440
Ow, it hurts.

849
42:25.260 --> 42:27.040
Are you two a couple?

850
42:27.860 --> 42:28.950
No.

851
42:29.240 --> 42:30.240
What makes you say that?

852
42:31.650 --> 42:32.970
I'm sorry.

853
42:32.990 --> 42:35.770
Uh... You two seem very close.

854
42:37.870 --> 42:39.480
Jaab and I are friends.

855
42:39.930 --> 42:42.110
He's my close friend.

856
42:47.040 --> 42:49.200
I'm sorry again for being mistaken.

857
42:55.000 --> 42:56.320
Jaab! Khanoon!

858
43:00.630 --> 43:01.460
Come here.

859
43:01.480 --> 43:03.140
- What the fuck do you want?! - What? What?

860
43:03.160 --> 43:03.900
Khanoon!

861
43:03.930 --> 43:05.440
Whoa, Sis!

862
43:05.460 --> 43:06.120
What is it?

863
43:06.140 --> 43:07.440
Oh, Sis...

864
43:08.160 --> 43:09.120
Pun!

865
43:09.600 --> 43:11.630
What the fuck are you doing?!

866
43:13.910 --> 43:14.720
Look.

867
43:24.050 --> 43:25.080
How cute.

868
43:28.830 --> 43:32.080
And why did you tell us to stop singing?

869
43:33.160 --> 43:36.520
And who did you call cute? Huh?!

870
43:37.150 --> 43:38.440
It was Ai.

871
43:39.160 --> 43:41.200
Would it be wrong if I wanted to make a move on him?

872
43:41.750 --> 43:43.080
If you aren't dating him

873
43:43.550 --> 43:46.030
and if he's single, that means he can be pursued by anyone.

874
43:46.430 --> 43:48.520
But isn't this a bit too early?

875
43:49.150 --> 43:50.470
Uh... You’re right.

876
43:50.490 --> 43:52.360
Isn't this a bit too early?

877
43:55.480 --> 43:56.550
Pun, my dear brother.

878
43:57.560 --> 43:59.760
What makes you so sure of your feelings

879
44:00.060 --> 44:01.520
that you are able to say it out loud?

880
44:12.850 --> 44:13.960
Are you alright?

881
44:14.660 --> 44:16.360
Who told you to drink that much?

882
44:18.140 --> 44:19.280
Oh, Jane.

883
44:21.490 --> 44:22.160
I'm drunk.

884
44:22.180 --> 44:24.050
Hey, Jane. Jane.

885
44:27.950 --> 44:28.950
I know.

886
44:32.450 --> 44:34.600
Don't tell Auntie Kaew.

887
44:36.860 --> 44:38.760
Why would I tell her?

888
44:39.360 --> 44:40.530
Are you leaving?

889
44:40.550 --> 44:41.560
I'll call you a ride.

890
44:44.660 --> 44:45.440
Jaab.

891
44:46.050 --> 44:46.840
Hm?

892
44:48.150 --> 44:51.580
Have you ever... loved someone?

893
44:52.770 --> 44:54.160
Have you ever been in a relationship?

894
44:56.150 --> 44:57.000
Jane...

895
44:57.740 --> 44:58.740
Why did you ask me that?

896
45:00.060 --> 45:01.440
When you feel that you...

897
45:02.240 --> 45:03.920
love someone

898
45:04.650 --> 45:06.440
who isn't your family,

899
45:06.740 --> 45:08.360
not a tree,

900
45:09.070 --> 45:10.440
not Auntie Kaew,

901
45:11.280 --> 45:12.560
what does it feel like?

902
45:15.250 --> 45:16.000
You...

903
45:17.480 --> 45:19.080
Are you...

904
45:23.380 --> 45:24.520
having...

905
45:26.160 --> 45:27.520
a crush on someone?

906
45:31.460 --> 45:32.680
I don't know.

907
45:33.440 --> 45:34.800
I'm not really sure.

908
45:35.750 --> 45:36.680
Jane...

909
45:37.060 --> 45:38.480
Who are you talking about?

910
45:41.150 --> 45:42.440
Is it...

911
45:44.270 --> 45:45.640
Is it me?

912
45:56.050 --> 45:58.160
What makes you so sure of your feelings

913
45:58.550 --> 46:00.080
that you are able to say it out loud?

914
46:12.400 --> 46:13.440
Hello.

915
46:13.950 --> 46:15.260
I'm Jane.

916
46:15.280 --> 46:16.520
It's my first day here.

917
46:17.050 --> 46:17.880
Oh.

918
46:19.040 --> 46:19.920
I'm Jaab.

919
46:24.350 --> 46:26.760
My heart’s been racing since the moment I first saw him.

920
46:30.180 --> 46:31.050
It's been racing like...

921
46:31.370 --> 46:32.570
The closer we get, the faster my heart races.

922
46:38.070 --> 46:39.960
I want to see him again and again.

923
46:41.950 --> 46:43.370
My gut is telling me that...

924
46:44.790 --> 46:46.000
it was love at first sight.

925
46:52.750 --> 46:55.800
Jane didn't make me fall for him slowly over time.

926
46:57.430 --> 46:59.360
I've been in love with him since the very start.

927
47:04.180 --> 47:05.180
Jane,

928
47:05.960 --> 47:07.170
I like you...

929
47:07.660 --> 47:09.240
so fucking much.

930
47:21.950 --> 47:22.720
Jaab.

931
47:23.350 --> 47:24.250
Hm?

932
47:24.850 --> 47:26.240
Have you ever been in a relationship?

933
47:27.660 --> 47:28.600
Jane...

934
47:29.260 --> 47:30.360
Why did you ask me that?

935
47:30.640 --> 47:32.140
When you feel that you...

936
47:32.760 --> 47:34.640
love someone

937
47:35.060 --> 47:36.330
what does it feel like?

938
47:36.730 --> 47:38.200
Are you...

939
47:38.330 --> 47:39.840
having...

940
47:41.350 --> 47:42.880
a crush on someone?

941
47:43.650 --> 47:44.920
I don't know.

942
47:45.560 --> 47:47.040
I'm not really sure.

943
47:48.010 --> 47:48.960
Jane...

944
47:49.350 --> 47:50.640
Who are you talking about?

945
47:51.550 --> 47:52.880
Is it...

946
47:53.560 --> 47:54.960
Is it me?

947
47:56.280 --> 47:57.040
Whoa?

948
47:59.260 --> 48:00.160
Who's there?

949
48:00.550 --> 48:01.800
What? Khanoon?

950
48:03.160 --> 48:04.200
Jaab.

951
48:04.580 --> 48:06.080
What the fuck are you doing here?

952
48:06.340 --> 48:07.340
I...

953
48:07.580 --> 48:08.800
Ugh, fuck.

954
48:08.950 --> 48:09.950
Jane, Jane.

955
48:09.970 --> 48:10.880
Hold on tight, okay?

956
48:10.920 --> 48:12.200
Don't let go, or you'll fall down.

957
48:14.060 --> 48:15.600
Damn it, Khanoon.

958
48:15.840 --> 48:17.700
Why the fuck are you drinking this much?!

959
48:18.940 --> 48:19.960
Fuck.

960
48:21.010 --> 48:22.140
No...

961
48:23.980 --> 48:25.200
It's not you, Jaab.

962
48:26.880 --> 48:28.400
Gosh, Khanoon!

963
48:32.370 --> 48:35.200
If somebody was to start having feelings for another person,

964
48:37.110 --> 48:38.320
this would be it.

965
48:44.280 --> 48:46.490
- There. So squishy. - Ow, ow, ow. It hurts!

966
48:46.520 --> 48:47.890
Both of us...

967
48:47.910 --> 48:49.570
have so much in common, don't we?

968
48:49.590 --> 48:52.220
At a glance, it might seem like we wouldn't get along,

969
48:52.250 --> 48:55.160
but we've got so much in common.

970
48:57.810 --> 49:00.200
Do you believe in the chemistry between two people?
